<%# locals: source — which page's signup this is (subscription_form's id and
    the subscriber's recorded source).

    A page's title block with the email signup beside it — the page renders
    this as a layout around its title, h1 through as-of line:
    render layout: "shared/headline_row", locals: { source: "senate" } do … end

    Beside the title from laptop width up, where that costs no height, and
    under it on narrower screens, where it costs one row. That's the one spot
    that clears the fold on every phone and laptop: below the title, the
    pages' own content — cards, maps, tables — fills the first screen. %>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-4 lg:flex-row lg:items-end lg:justify-between">
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
  <div class="lg:w-[26rem] lg:shrink-0">
    <%= render "shared/subscription_form", source: source, layout: "inline" %>
  </div>
</div>
